# Go SSR local rules

- Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/engineering/architecture.md`, and
  `docs/engineering/database.md`; they are authoritative.
- Keep Handler -> Service -> Repo: Handler owns HTTP, Service owns business
  rules/authorization/transactions, Repo owns data access.
- A Handler MUST NOT access `gorm.DB`; a Repo MUST NOT import Gin or decide
  permissions/business state. Pass `context.Context` below Handler.
- Complex action/workbench capabilities are not forced into CRUD symmetry.
- Bind request structs rather than scattering query/form reads. New fetch writes
  use JSON, CSRF, real HTTP methods, and a consistent JSON response.
- Parameterize SQL and select required columns. List queries filter, sort, count,
  and paginate in the DB unless a documented bounded dataset proves otherwise.
- ZenTao models match the existing ZenTao schema. `BaseModel`, `deletedAt`, and
  Workbench audit fields apply only to Workbench-owned tables.
- Use lower-case idiomatic file names; capability/layer underscores are allowed.
  Split by responsibility. First-party files SHOULD be <=300 and MUST be <=500
  lines unless recorded in the exact quality baseline; baseline files may not
  grow.
- Go unit tests remain beside the package as `*_test.go`; see
  `docs/engineering/testing.md` for integration/E2E boundaries.
- Never copy `internal/module/user/` as a Golden Reference; it is legacy and
  non-authoritative.
